  "why": "The causeway's program edited to stand a second lamp post in a middle column of the road, half-way along its run. The causeway declares itself a way six columns wide, so its run is judged at every station along its whole length, where no seam and no approach reaches: the post takes one of the six columns at its station, the rest stay clear, and every route proof passes beside it. Its own lamp post stands on the verge, outside the six, and is not judged. It declares no unit: what must not compile is a road narrowed along its length."
